---
/*
 * The product name as it is written wherever it can be styled: Yard, a bold U, luv.
 * Titles, meta descriptions, alt text and aria labels keep the plain string "YardUluv".
 * set:html keeps the markup on one line: a formatter that wraps the span would put
 * spaces inside the name. The site check reads .brand as one word.
 */
---

<span class="brand" set:html="Yard<b>U</b>luv" />
